That's step one. The emerald will take 8 turns. Of course, as soon as the
wraith stops fleeing, he'll zap you again, so standing on E is no help.
Striking while its back is turned might be an idea, but I'd prefer to get
some solid walls between me and it - hopefully the corridor beside you
leads into a zigzag.

I take it none of your un-id'ed potions are price-checked or clear? Drop
(or bag) any you're not going to throw, because boiling and explosion will
be your biggest risk. Hold only the extra healing, unless you have enough
Power to cast the spell a couple times; if so, drop them too.

Sleep has no effect on the undead, so forget the wand and harp. And, alas,
healing has no perverse damage effect on the undead--unlike in some other
games. So really it's stand or run, and keep healing yourself.

